window.__meadowSearchReceiveShard([{"t":"t006 - embedded media","p":"t006%20-%20embedded%20media.html","b":"PNG test embed in table Image Sizes Obsidian sizes an image with a width (|100, above) or a width and height (|100x50, here): In Markdown image syntax the size goes where the alt text goes, optionally after the alt text and a |. A local image, 80 pixels wide, with alt text: An external image, 250 pixels wide, with no alt text: Animated GIF test embed in table Too Big PNG link not tracked link not tracked test embed in table link not tracked SVG test embed in table with a container directive that makes the SVG's links interactive ⛶ Excalidraw link not tracked with a container directive that causes the links to be functional link not tracked enableEmbeddedLinks: true enableFullscreenButton: true enableOpenDedicatedPage: false test embed in table link not tracked t006 --- page that embeds Excalidraw in another directory Audio, video, and PDF Obsidian embeds audio and video with a player. These are a quarter-second tone and two seconds of green, kept small on purpose. The video is displayed at 320 by 180 pixels so its player controls are usable. A PDF embeds as a viewer, here opened at its first page and 200 pixels high. Its links work, and one goes to a page in this bundle, so that page is in the graph too. The icon at the top right opens the PDF's own page. Loading PDF…⤢ A container directive can give the viewer a fullscreen button: Loading PDF…⛶⤢"},{"t":"t008 - page conf do not include inlinks","p":"t008%20-%20page%20conf%20do%20not%20include%20inlinks.html","b":""}]);
